# Performance and Storage

- Optimize from measurements; do not replace AVFoundation/VideoToolbox with custom rendering without benchmark evidence.
- Pause decoding for sleep, display sleep, lock, invisible previews, serious thermal pressure, and configured low-power policy.
- Poll resource metrics only while a diagnostics surface observes them; bound all in-memory histories.
- Never decode a full master to render a library tile; use verified poster and preview variants.
- Import into a staging transaction, verify outputs, then atomically install metadata and files.
- Cancellation and crashes leave no library-visible partial asset and no permanent orphan.
- The agent is the sole persistent-state writer; SQLite uses migrations, foreign keys, and transactional changes.
- Binary media stays outside SQLite. Every stored file is referenced by metadata or an active staging journal.
- Use APFS cloning for compatible lock-screen installation when safe; fall back to copy and never hard-link user library media.
- Teardown is idempotent and releases windows, players, loopers, layers, observations, tasks, files, and descriptors.
- Preserve a poster during pause/failure so stopping decode does not produce a blank desktop.
- New continuous background work requires a measured energy budget and an off/suspend path.
